cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, datasets, or the CA-CRS+ framework, please cite it as below."
title: "CA-CRS+: A Zone-Aware, Resource-Informed Crowd Risk Scoring Framework with Cause-Specific Gate Intervention Recommendation for Stampede Prevention"
authors:
  - family-names: "Yadav"
    given-names: "Priyanshu Kumar"
    email: "priyanshu322006@gmail.com"
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Rajkiya Engineering College, Mainpuri, Uttar Pradesh, India"
  - family-names: "Mishra"
    given-names: "Abhinav Kumar"
    email: "mishrakabhinav34@gmail.com"
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Rajkiya Engineering College, Mainpuri, Uttar Pradesh, India"
abstract: "CA-CRS+ is a zone-aware, resource-informed crowd-risk scoring framework operating on standard RGB video without thermal cameras or cloud dependency. It introduces benchmark-validated crowd counting, directional conflict index via circular variance of optical flow, a non-linear crush scoring formula capturing zero-velocity gridlock, cause-to-gate recommendation with ripple-effect prevention, dynamic logarithmic personnel allocation, and multi-camera Global Risk Score fusion."
keywords:
  - "crowd safety"
  - "stampede prevention"
  - "zone-aware risk scoring"
  - "crowd counting"
  - "optical flow"
  - "causal attribution"
  - "gate intervention"
  - "multi-camera fusion"
  - "low-infrastructure public safety"
